          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for a share, then the Marathi for to be left over."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: बिघाड",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बिघाड — bighāḍ — \"a breakdown; a fault\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इंजिनात बिघाड झाल्यामुळे गाडी थांबली. iñjināt bighāḍ jhālyāmuḷe gāḍī thāmblī. The train stopped because of a fault in the engine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बिघाड (bighāḍ) होणे, a fault occurs; the place of the fault takes -त. The verb is बिघडणे, to go wrong."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बिघाड (bighāḍ) is inherited, from the family of Sanskrit vighaṭate, \"flies apart, is broken\", where CDIAL lists Marathi bighaḍṇẽ, \"to be spoilt\" (CDIAL 11673)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
